# Owner dashboard — do not revert

The premium owner area is **committed and intentional**. Do not undo it while "fixing" other issues.

## Never do without explicit user request

- `git checkout`, `git restore`, or `git reset` on `src/components/dashboard/**`, `src/app/dashboard/**`, `src/lib/owner-*.ts`, `src/lib/listing-workspace*.ts`, `src/components/dashboard/listing-workspace/**`, `src/components/dashboard/owner-home/**`, `ShortTermCalendarHub.tsx`, or related owner UI
- `Delete` on any of the files above
- Replacing the **left sidebar** (`AccountNav` + `DashboardProfileCard` in `DashboardShell`) without explicit user request
- Replacing **property card grid** default with list-only / table CRM layout

## Expected owner UI (baseline)

- **DashboardShell**: top nav (`OwnerTopNav` in header) + main content — **no left sidebar**
- **DashboardHeader**: logo + top nav tabs + CTA/profile
- **Listings**: `DashboardListingGridCard` default; Cards/List toggle
- **Home**: `OwnerHomeOverview` on `/dashboard`
- **Listing workspace**: tabs under `/dashboard/listings/[id]/*`
- **Short-term only**: `ShortTermCalendarHub` on availability tab (daily prices in cells + `ShortTermDailyPriceTable`)

## If UI looks wrong

1. Confirm URL is **owner dashboard**, not public site:
   - Owner: `http://localhost:3000/dashboard/listings` and `/dashboard/listings/[id]`
   - Public (unchanged): `/`, `/listings` — different design by design
2. Assume **stale cache** — run `npm run dev:restart:clean` and hard refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R)
3. Fix the **specific bug** in place; do not bulk-revert
3. Restore from checkpoint only if user asks: `npm run checkpoint:list` then `npm run checkpoint:restore`

## After meaningful owner UI changes

Remind user to run `npm run checkpoint -- -Label "description"` if they want an extra backup outside git.
